nterviewer: Why do we use redis-cli instead of bash to access Redis?

Answer:

bash or sh is a Linux shell used to interact with the container's operating system. redis-cli is a Redis client that communicates with the Redis server using the Redis protocol.
Linux commands (ls, pwd) work in the shell, while Redis commands (PING, SET, GET) work in redis-cli.

This distinction applies to many other applications too:

MySQL → mysql
PostgreSQL → psql
MongoDB → mongosh
Redis → redis-cli

In each case, you first enter the container with kubectl exec, then use the application's own client to communicate with that application.

