Interview answer ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
If an interviewer asks:
"What happens to a Service when a Pod is deleted?"

The Service keeps the same ClusterIP and NodePort.
When the Deployment creates a replacement Pod with a new IP address,
Kubernetes automatically updates the Service's endpoints.
Clients continue to access the Service without knowing that the Pod IP changed."

Pod IP = 10.244.0.6	                  New Pod IP = 10.244.0.9
Endpoints include 10.244.0.6	        Endpoints include 10.244.0.9
Service IP = 10.96.120.50	            Same 10.96.120.50
NodePort = 31234	                    Same 31234
Users can access the app	            Users can still access the app

Only the Pod IP changes.
The Service remains the same and automatically starts sending traffic to the new Pod.
